<onlyinclude>'''Swarm intelligence''' describes collective problem solving or coordinated behavior arising from interactions among many relatively simple individuals. Researchers study natural examples and engineer algorithms inspired by them.

== Explanation ==
Ants can collectively establish routes through local interactions, while simulated particles can cooperate to search a difficult optimization space. There need not be a single individual that controls every action. Not every coordinated group or distributed program is a swarm.

